  "id": "Compound::DB00148 - Gene::6535",
  "verbalization": "Creatine is linked to Slc6a8 through a shared pathway involving creatine metabolism, as evidenced by multiple paths that demonstrate a bidirectional relationship between Creatine and the transporter Ckmt1a, Ckmt1b, or Ckmt2. These transporters are all involved in the metabolic processes of Creatine, which are ultimately associated with Slc6a8. The evidence suggests that Creatine interacts with these transporters, which in turn participate in the metabolic pathways that lead to the interaction with Slc6a8. This indicates a potential mechanism where Creatine influences Slc6a8 through its role in the metabolic regulation of creatine transporters. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust connection, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
